1
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:12,030
[Where are you? I'll come get you]

2
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:38,690
Morning.

3
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,540
Morning.

4
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:47,080
Want me to come get you after work?

5
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,100
No, it's fine.

6
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,140
I'll be heading straight home today.

7
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:55,000
Then can we eat dinner together?

8
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:57,380
Sure.

9
00:00:57,380 --> 00:00:58,950
Great.

10
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:31,220
- Your key?
- Yeah... Oh.

11
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:32,860
Thanks.

12
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:36,350
Huh?

13
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:40,460
Oh, sorry.

14
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:43,600
It's fine. Thanks.

15
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:47,050
See you later.

16
00:01:53,670 --> 00:01:55,240
Eita?

17
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:59,400
Could you take time off work today?

18
00:02:00,490 --> 00:02:02,230
Is everything okay?

19
00:02:07,750 --> 00:02:10,780
Sorry. It's nothing.

20
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:14,190
Take care.

21
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,200
[4 years ago - Japan]

22
00:04:11,410 --> 00:04:13,440
Hello, it's your neighbor.

23
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:18,170
I promise I'm no one suspicious.

24
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:42,550
I'll be next door.

25
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:51,790
I can't do much, but I am a neighbor.

26
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:58,670
I'll leave the door open when I'm home.

27
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,080
That's all.

28
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:05,720
Good night.

29
00:06:15,410 --> 00:06:17,690
Mr. Nishikido?

30
00:06:17,690 --> 00:06:19,340
Ms. Tan Lei.

31
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,710
We met at Xiufang's shop.

32
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:24,920
Yes. I'm Sakura's partner.

33
00:06:25,650 --> 00:06:27,660
I manage the artworks left here.

34
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,810
Would you like to see inside?

35
00:06:28,810 --> 00:06:31,520
No. Just the outside today.

36
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,180
I see.

37
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,680
Has there been any trouble
selling this building?

38
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:44,200
Would you feel better if it were gone?

39
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:49,580
Sometimes, I think so too.

40
00:06:53,110 --> 00:06:55,540
I don't need to see inside.

41
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,240
You want to go on without seeing it?

42
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:52,830
What is this?

43
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:58,410
He's drawn this many times since the accident.

44
00:07:59,130 --> 00:08:01,680
Did he remember this room?

45
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,900
No.

46
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:09,700
He thought it was a place he had never seen.

47
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:15,410
He kept drawing the same woman.

48
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,610
Without knowing who she was.

49
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:25,410
When did he realize it was Sakura?

50
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,930
After he met her again.

51
00:08:33,910 --> 00:08:36,230
Even though he forgot...

52
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:42,680
He never stopped drawing.

53
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:47,770
That's why you don't want them
to see each other.

54
00:08:47,770 --> 00:08:50,800
Why did she come back here again?

55
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,750
She doesn't remember anything.

56
00:08:53,750 --> 00:08:55,650
Wait.

57
00:08:55,650 --> 00:08:59,370
She doesn't remember?

58
00:08:59,370 --> 00:09:04,460
Her memories of the time she spent with Lun
faded little by little.

59
00:09:06,910 --> 00:09:09,840
She's not pretending to have forgotten.

60
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:20,250
But even without remembering,

61
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:27,020
they both came back to the same place.

62
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:44,810
I've watched Sakura for the last four years.

63
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:47,010
And I've watched Lun.

64
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,070
Then you understand.

65
00:09:50,070 --> 00:09:52,210
I don't know what's right.

66
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:04,060
Excuse me.

67
00:10:34,610 --> 00:10:37,400
Your face looks terrible.

68
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:39,350
Yeah?

69
00:10:39,350 --> 00:10:41,370
You look like you haven't slept.

70
00:10:45,910 --> 00:10:49,340
So? Did something happen?

71
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,160
I saw them.

72
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,800
Saw who?

73
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,470
Your girlfriend?

74
00:11:05,050 --> 00:11:06,950
Ask her about it.

75
00:11:06,950 --> 00:11:08,300
I can't.

76
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:10,180
Why not?

77
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:14,700
Because asking might end everything.

78
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:22,810
At least she still comes home.

79
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:29,010
I envy Sakura.

80
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:31,340
What?

81
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:35,710
She's lucky to have someone
who's so scared of losing her.

82
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:43,610
Maybe she's "coming home",
only because she has to.

83
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:11,250
Come on in.

84
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:29,650
You can leave the door open.

85
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:32,060
What?

86
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:34,560
I'm a stranger, and a man.

87
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:37,110
You should be able to leave
if you ever feel uncomfortable.

88
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:42,810
Not that I plan on doing anything, of course.

89
00:12:46,570 --> 00:12:48,710
Are you hungry?

90
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:52,780
A bit.

91
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,810
Then come eat.

92
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:42,700
I'm so sorry. I can't believe I fell asleep.

93
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:45,920
It's fine.

94
00:13:46,470 --> 00:13:48,360
Feel free to sleep all you want.

95
00:13:55,090 --> 00:13:59,830
You're always welcome to relax at my place.

96
00:13:59,830 --> 00:14:03,140
You can leave at any time as well.

97
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,420
See?

98
00:14:06,190 --> 00:14:08,630
The door is still open for you.

99
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,330
Please...

100
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:18,220
Don't feel obligated to help.

101
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:20,130
Obligated?

102
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:26,020
You have no reason to help me.

103
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:31,000
Do I need a reason to lend a hand?

104
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:37,070
You'll only exhaust yourself, and fast.

105
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:42,110
Helping others...

106
00:14:43,490 --> 00:14:45,580
It's tiring.

107
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:52,000
Then I'll tell you if I ever tire out.

108
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:59,010
I want to see you fully recover, Ms. Sakura.

109
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:03,820
<i>I didn't want to tie her down.</i>

110
00:15:04,830 --> 00:15:09,540
<i>I just wanted to become
a place she could call home.</i>

111
00:15:10,690 --> 00:15:13,860
[How about nikujaga for dinner?]

112
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,360
You still have to make some.

113
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:34,950
There's already a lot, though.

114
00:15:50,760 --> 00:16:03,700
[White pepper]

115
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:07,670
[Lun's Secret Recipe]
[White pepper is key]

116
00:16:15,950 --> 00:16:18,620
- I'm home.
- Welcome back.

117
00:16:21,090 --> 00:16:22,520
You're cooking today?

118
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,210
Yeah.

119
00:16:24,210 --> 00:16:28,010
White pepper? That's an unusual pick.

120
00:16:28,010 --> 00:16:29,150
Really?

121
00:16:29,150 --> 00:16:32,540
Yeah. I don't see you use it often.

122
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:38,800
How about I cook for us instead?

123
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,230
No, I want to...

124
00:16:40,230 --> 00:16:42,300
I can't have you overexerting yourself.

125
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:43,980
Just leave it to me.

126
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,820
Are you tired?

127
00:17:02,950 --> 00:17:04,620
No.

128
00:17:09,490 --> 00:17:11,680
Tell me if anything's wrong, okay?

129
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,510
I'll be here to listen.

130
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:18,670
Okay.

131
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,210
Sakura.

132
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,000
Sorry.

133
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:46,520
No, it's just... I'm tired.

134
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:50,040
Yeah. I know.

135
00:18:02,870 --> 00:18:05,080
<i>I want us to go back to normal, and yet...</i>

136
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:28,740
What are you drawing?

137
00:18:34,190 --> 00:18:35,870
I don't know.

138
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:40,260
You met her again?

139
00:18:52,730 --> 00:18:54,400
Did I...

140
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:58,830
Did I love her?

141
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:10,210
Don't you already know the answer?

142
00:19:14,770 --> 00:19:16,620
Erase that sketch.

143
00:19:29,930 --> 00:19:32,100
This is my hand.

144
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:37,470
Did I hurt her?

145
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:43,350
Why can't I remember anything?

146
00:19:44,830 --> 00:19:46,620
Why?

147
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:09,160
[Keep this, until I want to remember]

148
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:14,930
[Lun]

149
00:20:14,930 --> 00:20:16,210
"Lun".

150
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:23,930
"203".

151
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:27,180
[Accident - Rain]
[Ambulance - Red Lights]

152
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:30,190
"An accident". "Rain".

153
00:20:31,820 --> 00:20:33,990
[Day 3: I still remember his voice]

154
00:20:33,990 --> 00:20:36,440
"I still remember his voice".

155
00:20:37,510 --> 00:20:39,780
[Day 10: His voice sounds far]
[Trying to remember hurts my head]

156
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,940
"His voice sounds far".

157
00:20:42,970 --> 00:20:45,330
[One month: His face is a blur]
[Yet my chest hurts]

158
00:20:45,330 --> 00:20:47,620
"His face is a blur".

159
00:20:48,270 --> 00:20:51,270
[Three months: I can't remember his name]
[without writing it out]

160
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:53,340
"I can't remember".

161
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:55,930
[6 months: Who is it I've forgotten?]
[Did I really want to forget?]

162
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:59,030
"Who is it I've forgotten?"

163
00:20:59,570 --> 00:21:02,240
[It's not that I've forgotten]
[Every day, he gets further away]

164
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:04,750
"It's not that I've forgotten".

165
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:08,520
"Every day, he gets further away".

166
00:21:11,670 --> 00:21:14,110
"Eita. I entrust this truth to you."

167
00:21:14,110 --> 00:21:17,070
"The truth, of the day I broke."

168
00:21:18,810 --> 00:21:26,220
[But the key to 203]
[is the one thing I can't give you]

169
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:32,680
<i>She couldn't entrust me with 203.</i>

170
00:22:02,620 --> 00:22:05,140
<i>You can leave the door open.</i>

171
00:22:06,540 --> 00:22:07,550
<i>What?</i>

172
00:22:07,550 --> 00:22:09,920
<i>You should be able to leave
if you ever feel uncomfortable.</i>

173
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:44,050
I'll leave the door open.

174
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:59,050
[Next]
